"Vapour-compression refrigeration cycle with R134a, states 1 to 4

 Evaporator 4 -> 1, compressor 1 -> 2, condenser 2 -> 3, expansion valve 3 -> 4. The cycle is
 specified by its saturation temperatures, superheat and subcooling, and its cooling capacity:
 the refrigerant mass flow is a result.

 Also in this project:
   Cycle diagram   the flowsheet with the four components
   Parametric      COP and compressor power over the evaporating temperature
   Plots           P-h diagram (logarithmic pressure axis) and COP against T_evap
   Goal seek       condensing temperature for a COP of 4"

"The unit system: C, bar, kJ, kg/s"
$UnitSystem Eng

"---------------------------------------------------------------- inputs"
T_evap = -10 [C]               "evaporating temperature"
T_cond = 40 [C]                "condensing temperature"
dT_sh = 5 [dK]                 "superheat at the compressor inlet (a temperature difference: dK)"
dT_sc = 3 [dK]                 "subcooling at the condenser outlet"
eta_c = 0.75                   "compressor isentropic efficiency"
Q_evap = 10 [kW]               "cooling capacity"

"---------------------------------------------------------------- states
 Saturation pressures from the saturation temperatures (pressure losses neglected)"
P[1] = p_sat(R134a, T=T_evap)
P[2] = p_sat(R134a, T=T_cond)
P[3] = P[2]
P[4] = P[1]

"1: superheated vapour leaving the evaporator"
T[1] = T_evap + dT_sh
h[1] = enthalpy(R134a, T=T[1], P=P[1])
s[1] = entropy(R134a, T=T[1], P=P[1])

"2: compressor outlet"
h_s[2] = enthalpy(R134a, P=P[2], s=s[1])
eta_c = (h_s[2] - h[1]) / (h[2] - h[1])
T[2] = temperature(R134a, P=P[2], h=h[2])
s[2] = entropy(R134a, P=P[2], h=h[2])

"3: subcooled liquid leaving the condenser"
T[3] = T_cond - dT_sc
h[3] = enthalpy(R134a, T=T[3], P=P[3])
s[3] = entropy(R134a, T=T[3], P=P[3])

"4: the expansion valve is isenthalpic; the refrigerant enters the evaporator as a wet mixture"
h[4] = h[3]
T[4] = temperature(R134a, P=P[4], h=h[4])
x[4] = quality(R134a, P=P[4], h=h[4])
s[4] = entropy(R134a, P=P[4], h=h[4])

"One refrigerant flow through the whole cycle"
Duplicate i = 1, 4
  m[i] = m_dot
End

"---------------------------------------------------------------- performance
 Q_evap is given, so this equation determines the mass flow m_dot."
Q_evap = m[4]*(h[1] - h[4])    {kW}
W_c = m[1]*(h[2] - h[1])       {kW}
Q_cond = m[2]*(h[2] - h[3])    {kW}
COP = Q_evap/W_c               "coefficient of performance"
COP_carnot = (T_evap + 273.15)/(T_cond - T_evap)    "Carnot COP between the saturation temperatures"
eta_II = COP/COP_carnot        "second-law efficiency"
